[{"id":80036,"sender_id":782,"sender_full_name":"Dean","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/090f23599434446cd0a388971e8dfa83?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/.22Algebraic.20Real.20Analysis.22.20and.20Freyd.27s.20theory.20of.20Scales/near/80036\">#1</a> We don’t have an article on Peter Freyd’s “algebraic real analysis”. This is related to Tom Leinster’s characterization of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L^1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> as well. It’s all very interesting work, and it leads to clean proofs of e.g. existence and uniqueness of Haar measure. I was hoping to make an article about these things on Wednesday if that is ok.</p>","timestamp":1574723815,"subject":"\"Algebraic Real Analysis\" and Freyd's theory of Scales","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":80038,"sender_id":29,"sender_full_name":"Todd_Trimble","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/078428beaeaddf058781b9be6b2c240f?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/.22Algebraic.20Real.20Analysis.22.20and.20Freyd.27s.20theory.20of.20Scales/near/80038\">#2</a> Sure, give it a go!</p>","timestamp":1574731548,"subject":"\"Algebraic Real Analysis\" and Freyd's theory of Scales","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":80064,"sender_id":147,"sender_full_name":"Dmitri Pavlov","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7c66d1b7cad17c58076e0f3d13220d63?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/.22Algebraic.20Real.20Analysis.22.20and.20Freyd.27s.20theory.20of.20Scales/near/80064\">#3</a> I'd be interested to see at least some references on this matter.</p>","timestamp":1574798873,"subject":"\"Algebraic Real Analysis\" and Freyd's theory of Scales","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":80149,"sender_id":782,"sender_full_name":"Dean","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/090f23599434446cd0a388971e8dfa83?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/.22Algebraic.20Real.20Analysis.22.20and.20Freyd.27s.20theory.20of.20Scales/near/80149\">#4</a> Looks like I won’t be free to write it for about half a month. For now, here are two references:</p>\n<p>1) <a href=\"http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/20/10/20-10.pdf\">Peter Freyd’s Algebraic Real Analysis</a></p>\n<p>2) <a href=\"https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~tl/cambridge_ct14/cambridge_ct14_talk.pdf\">Tom Leinster’s characterization of  L^1 </a></p>\n<p>I think it is also related to convex sets and the <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Giry%2Bmonad\">Giry+monad</a>.</p>","timestamp":1575089909,"subject":"\"Algebraic Real Analysis\" and Freyd's theory of Scales","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]}]